olled by a regulatory-industrial cartel. The insistence on silicon-level verification assumes that institutional gatekeepers can impartially hold the cryptographic keys without abusing them to suppress open-source competition. When technical standards are fused with hardware monopolies, who audits the auditors holding the root keys?",
